# NiyamNetra env template — copy to .env for local overrides.
# .env itself stays git-ignored (see .gitignore); only this example is committed.
#
# You normally do NOT need this file: backend switching is a runtime choice on
# the login screen (Local / LAN / Render / Custom, remembered across restarts),
# and LAN is auto-detected from the Metro dev-server host.
#
# Set the var below ONLY to force one fixed backend at build time (it is
# inlined into the bundle — restart Metro with `npx expo start -c` after any
# change, and it cannot be changed in an installed APK; prefer eas.json
# per-profile env for APK builds).
#
# Single source of truth for the fallback host is api/config.js (FALLBACK_HOST).
# This file and eas.json only ever override via EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL.
#
# Examples (no quotes, no trailing slash):
#   Android emulator (backend on same PC): http://10.0.2.2:8000
#   Another PC on the LAN:                 http://192.168.1.7:8000
#   Deployed backend:                      https://niyamnetra-backend.onrender.com
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.7:8000
